<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/actively-open-minded-thinking#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/actively-open-minded-thinking> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-04"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/actively-open-minded-thinking> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#Disposition> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/actively-open-minded-thinking> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Actively open-minded thinking" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/actively-open-minded-thinking> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "AOT" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/actively-open-minded-thinking> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "actively openminded thinking" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/actively-open-minded-thinking> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/thinking-dispositions> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/actively-open-minded-thinking> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A thinking disposition, named by Jonathan Baron, in which a person searches thoroughly and fairly for possibilities, evidence and goals, gives weight to evidence against a favoured view, and holds confidence in proportion to the search actually done." .
