<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/premortem#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/premortem> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-03"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/premortem> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#Technique> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/premortem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Premortem" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/premortem> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "pre-mortem analysis" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/premortem> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "pre-mortem" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/premortem> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "premortem analysis" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/premortem> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "project premortem" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/premortem> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/debiasing> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/premortem> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/structured-analytic-techniques> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/premortem> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A plan-evaluation technique in which a team, before committing to a plan, imagines that it has already been carried out and has failed, then has each member independently write down the reasons it failed so those risks can be addressed in advance." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/premortem> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/scheme/decision-making> .
