<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/posterior-analytics#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/posterior-analytics> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-03"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/posterior-analytics> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#Work> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/posterior-analytics> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Posterior Analytics" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/posterior-analytics> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Analytica Posteriora" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/posterior-analytics> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Aristotle's theory of demonstration" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/posterior-analytics> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/organon> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/posterior-analytics> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Aristotle's two-book treatise (4th century BCE) on demonstration and scientific knowledge, which argues that a proof yields knowledge only when its premises are true, primary and explanatory, and that the chain of proof must end in first principles grasped without demonstration." .
