  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/informal-fallacy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A recurring, deceptively bad pattern of argument whose flaw lies in its content, context or use (relevance, ambiguity, unwarranted assumption or dialogue misconduct) rather than in an invalid logical form that formal analysis alone could expose." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/informal-fallacy> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/scheme/informal-fallacies> .
