  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/justified-true-belief> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The proposal that a person knows a claim if and only if the claim is true, they believe it, and they are justified in believing it; long treated as the standard analysis of propositional knowledge until Gettier cases showed the three conditions are not jointly sufficient." .
