<https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/simpsons-paradox#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/simpsons-paradox> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-05"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/simpsons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/ontology#Phenomenon> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/simpsons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Simpson's paradox" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/simpsons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Simpson's reversal" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/simpsons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Yule-Simpson effect" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/simpsons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "amalgamation paradox" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/simpsons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "reversal paradox" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/simpsons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/statistical-paradox> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/simpsons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A statistical pattern in which an association between two variables that holds in a whole population weakens, vanishes or reverses direction once the population is split into subgroups, so that pooled and stratified data point to opposite conclusions." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/simpsons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/scheme/probabilistic-reasoning> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/simpsons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Simpson's paradox" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/simpsons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/base-rate-neglect> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/simpsons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/berksons-paradox> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/simpsons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/correlation-versus-causation> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/simpsons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/randomized-controlled-trial> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/simpsons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/sure-thing-principle> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/simpsons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/source/simpsons-paradox/s1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/simpsons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/critical-thinking-graph/id/source/simpsons-paradox/s2> .
